statement:
A nonzero ordinary ideal class at every higher level. Retain the fixed tower and the distinguished degree-one primes \(P_{2,0,n}\) of A.166. Then \[ [P_{2,0,n}]_{(3)}
e0 \quad\hbox{in }\operatorname{Cl}(K_n)\{3\} \qquad(n\geq3). 	ag{A.168.1} \] In particular no integral element of \(K_n\), for \(n\geq3\), has rational norm \(2\) or \(-2\). Let \(\mathcal F_{3,S}\) be the completed \(S\)-unit norm fibre \[ \mathcal F_{3,S}=\{x\in\widehat E_{3,3}: N_{K_3/\Q}x=[-2]\}. \] Its actual valuation map at the two quadratic changed-prime branches has the following proved image containment: \[  egin{gathered} 
u:\mathcal F_{3,S}\longrightarrow\Z_3^2, \qquad x\longmapsto(c_{11},c_{59}),\ 
u(\mathcal F_{3,S})\subset \{(b,c)\in\Z_3^2:c-4b\equiv3\pmod9\}. \end{gathered} 	ag{A.168.2} \] At either changed prime the full divisor vector is \((-2c_q,c_q)\), with the actual residue-degree weights \((1,2)\). The same constraint holds for the stable changed-prime coordinates of every unrestricted completed coherent norm family over \([-2]\), through A.166. In particular at least one of these coordinates has three-adic valuation at most one. For the balanced classes of A.155 one has the sharper bound \[ 3^{n-2}e_n=0\qquad(n\geq2). 	ag{A.168.3} \] The quotient map from the ordinary class group to \(C_n^{m bal}\) takes the nonzero class in A.168.1 to \(e_n\). Neither A.168.1 nor A.168.3 decides whether that image is zero. The balanced class \(e_3\), and the coherent norm fibre, remain unresolved by these assertions.
